WEBVTT

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.560
What's wrong?

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.750
So, you're heading to Mistral?

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.110
That sucks.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.450
But they do say the food and
women are good there.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.450
It's been six months
since the ceasefire.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.280
Glad we both made
it through alive!

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.860
Grand ouvert!
Read 'em and weep!

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.670
- You've gotta be kidding me!
- Damn!     - Seriously?

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.790
Miss! You up?

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.970
Your share of the spoils of war.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:27.770
Caramel?

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:32.230
I-I'm honored to receive
such a treasure!

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.070
Um, Sergeant!

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.200
Don't worry.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.110
If you're nice to the trumpeter,
you can hear them sound the retreat better.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.190
Odd to see a new recruit,
now that the draft's over.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:46.710
You volunteered?

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.320
Yes! I wanted to learn
how to play music.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.290
I mean...

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.500
An honest girl... I like that!
Good luck, kiddo!

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.530
Private, what's your name?

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:03.260
Kanata! Kanata Sorami!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:12.050
So Ra No Wo To

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.280
The Sound that Fills the Air -
The City of Dawn

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.240
Seize is having a festival today.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.490
A festival?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.530
So I can't take you further.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.530
Look.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.200
That's where you've been assigned.
Locals call it Clocktower Fortress.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.230
Set a course for it.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.370
Right!

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.850
Orders for Private Kanata Sorami.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:45.700
You are ordered to report to the
1121 Platoon in Seize City, Trois.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:49.280
Helvetia Republic Army HQ.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.710
As of 1320, this mission is complete!

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.030
Thank you very much!

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.020
The town of lakes
and glass, Seize.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.600
Wait! Wait!

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.380
I'm supposed to report at 1500.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:30.640
I can finally let you sing.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.380
Direction confirmed!

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.510
Time confirmed!

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:40.860
Equipment confirmed!

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.150
Advance!

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.640
Step right up!

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.230
G-flat... A wonderful sound!

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.870
Fishies!

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.660
Ten yen, twenty-five sen.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.420
What a beautiful doll-

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.780
I-I'm sorry!

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.040
What's wrong, Rio?

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:52.760
A kitten had too much fun at the fair,
and it ran off in the wrong direction.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.350
Can't be helped...

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.350
Cats always take their
time getting places.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.680
That's why they're
cute, you know.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.860
If it were a stray, it'd be OK.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:09.610
But it's a domesticated cat.

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:30.650
Wow, that scared me...

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.760
But I found another
wonderful thing.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.100
What's wrong?

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:45.190
Thanks!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.950
Hey! A soldier!

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.360
A girl from the fort?

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:00.740
Great!

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.240
To the Flame Maidens!

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:03.830
Thank you!

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:14.470
Thank you!

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.060
OK!

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.490
I'll get you for that!

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:30.570
Ready... Fire!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.420
Thanks!

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:34.320
Thanks!

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:58.010
Hey!

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.380
Are you stupid or something?

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:02.350
You shouldn't have joined them!

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.820
Your uniform's all messy now!

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:08.390
Umm... A-Ah...

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.360
God bless you.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.010
Thank...

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.870
Geez... Come with me!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.630
How's the bath?

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.270
It's great!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.910
That's good.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:46.610
Looks like you made quite the target...
Couldn't you have dodged a little?

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:53.610
Don't worry.
Once it dries, this dye fades.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.120
That's a festival, right?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.790
It comes from a Seize legend.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.390
A legend?

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:03.000
What kind of legend?

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:08.360
The legend of the Flame Maidens
who protect the city...

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.170
Sorry for the trouble.

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:22.340
I'll add it to your tab.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:24.510
I'm done with the repairs, too.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.200
And... This, too.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.170
Filicia...

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.030
That nosy brat!

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:40.000
Late.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.920
Late! Late!

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.900
<i>She's late!</i>

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:46.120
And we came to welcome her, too!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.060
Calm down.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.590
Let's relax and wait for her.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.100
It's a present from
your father, right?

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.710
It's nice.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.830
D-flat.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:03.050
Thank you for the bath!

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:07.580
Um... I get lost a lot.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:10.640
But thanks to that, I met
someone this wonderful!

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.310
You're welcome.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.280
But don't get lost here.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:23.500
Wow!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:30.740
You can tell the pitch?

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:41.860
It's a clear... somehow
nostalgic sound.

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.110
That's not what I meant!

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:46.880
Thief!

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.850
You idiot!

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.720
Thank you very much.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:57.860
Geez...

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.610
You'd die over something
like that?

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.670
But that bell...

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:06.960
It's fine.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.120
I'm sure this is for the best.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.340
She's late.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:22.970
Happiness.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:34.840
Um...

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:37.020
I've got something
to do, so I'm off.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.810
Don't get lost again.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:44.400
That bell... I'm sure it was
really important to her.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.270
What should I do?

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.540
Oh, no!

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.840
That way?

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:11.220
Advance!

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.390
The Flame Maidens?

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:15.410
A long time ago, before the world
became the way it is now,

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:22.810
a winged demon came to live
at the bottom of this valley.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:34.320
The demon breathed fire, shook the ground,
and caused people to suffer.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:42.420
Finally, he kidnapped the maidens
who lived in the fort,

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.740
locking them in an
underground labyrinth.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:55.350
The girls, however,
refused to give up,

00:14:55.350 --> 00:15:01.140
and called to each other with golden horns
given to them by the Lord of Heaven.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:06.990
Upon escaping the labyrinth,
they gained the help of an enormous spider

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:12.150
and defeated the demon, taking its head.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:16.920
Once they'd done so, it began
spewing flame everywhere.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:21.540
If nothing had been done, it would have
burned the town above to ash.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:30.060
To keep the flames at bay, the maidens embraced
the demon's head, each in turn.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:36.790
Every day, the villagers would throw water
on the maiden with the flaming head.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:40.590
A year passed, and the flames
disappeared at last.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.440
Thus, every year, the town celebrates
the water-throwing festival

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:49.300
to commemorate the maidens
who saved it.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.420
The new girl never came.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.570
Who cares?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.400
Captain, look at Rio-sempai!

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.150
You're right. She looks great.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:58.040
We were right to leave it to her.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.160
But we drew straws-

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.850
I got lost again.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.550
I'm a failure...

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:26.400
Sometimes, getting lost means
that something fun happens.

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:32.600
But that's only when you
meet someone new.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:38.500
It's no fun being alone.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:40.990
Are you lost?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.380
Yeah.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:44.240
I want my mommy!

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.250
Don't worry.

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:52.080
If you long for her, she'll know.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.240
Really?

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:56.370
A sound will always fill the air.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.760
Fill the air.

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.380
Fill the air...

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.370
And then, it reaches
people's ears.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:11.050
Here sleep the Flame Maidens.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:19.070
Awaken now, and embrace the
demon to quell its curse.

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:20.660
What?

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.820
The golden horns?

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:25.840
Has the demon awakened?

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:27.250
Kureha!

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:42.470
Please, someone... Hear my sound!

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.650
It reached them.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:03.470
Sound fills the air, and then...

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:08.040
Get out of bed!

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.380
Private Kanata Sorami!

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:19.010
Huh? Where am I?

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.620
Snap out of it, already.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.090
This is Clocktower Fortress,

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:25.100
base camp of the 1121 Platoon!

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:46.190
Um... I-I'm very sorry
about yesterday!

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:48.590
Damn right, you are.

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:50.300
I-I'm sorry!

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:52.180
But...

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.560
I'm kidding.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.850
But from now on,
don't do stuff like that.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.990
Not for something as
stupid as this bell.

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.760
Let me show you something.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:24.490
A trumpet!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:29.040
This is why we're called
Clocktower Fortress.

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:06.580
It's the sound of the sky!

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.020
Rio Kazumiya.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:46.020
That's my name.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:50.100
I'll teach you how to
play the trumpet.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:55.030
Thank you, Sergeant Rio-dono!

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:56.240
Rio's fine.

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:56.870
Huh?

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:58.130
Filicia.

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:03.820
The captain's policy is
not to use ranks here.

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:07.840
Uh... So, Rio-sempai!

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:12.530
Then let's get started.

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:14.820
Play a wake-up reveille!

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:34.870
The girl they've got playing this
morning isn't very good.

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:19.770
Next time: First Battle - A Chair Story!

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:24.760
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
